+- [#93](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/pull/93) [`a7faee0`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/a7faee013da49aa8415bad2da9f58be26e093fab) Thanks [@PazChen](https://github.com/PazChen)! - The chat takes any number of files in one message, and folders too. A file or folder dragged in from your disk stays where it is: the message gives the agent its path, and the agent copies into the project only what the film uses, so Studio's media no longer fills up with everything you dropped. A file pasted from the clipboard, which has no path of its own, is kept in the project's `.film/attachments/`. Up to 20 pictures go to the agent with a message, the pictures of what you pointed at in Studio first; the rest go by their path.
+
+- [#93](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/pull/93) [`a7faee0`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/a7faee013da49aa8415bad2da9f58be26e093fab) Thanks [@PazChen](https://github.com/PazChen)! - The chat leaves more room under its last message, and the way back to the latest is a round down arrow above the composer.
+
+- [#93](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/pull/93) [`a7faee0`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/a7faee013da49aa8415bad2da9f58be26e093fab) Thanks [@PazChen](https://github.com/PazChen)! - CodeBuddy works as its China edition: it is started that way unless your shell sets CODEBUDDY_INTERNET_ENVIRONMENT yourself, and its install link is the China site's. A turn an agent gives up on now shows the agent's own reason (CodeBuddy's network error, say) instead of an empty reply. Signing in in Terminal runs in a folder of OpenFilm's own, so CodeBuddy no longer warns about trusting your home folder. Two models an agent names alike (CodeBuddy's "Hy3") are told apart in the menu.
